  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the national response for the control of STI/HIV in Angola - Angola (01-Jul-2016-30-Jun-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Angola, HIV, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Angola)This program has the following goals: Strengthening the national response for the control of STI/HIV and viral Hepatitis to ensure an HIV prevalence rate of less than 3%. The objectives of this program are: Increase from 52% to 90% the follow-up of positive pregnant women on antiretroviral treatment (ART) by 2018.  Increase from 74% to 90% the percentage of male and female sex workers who report condom use with their last client 2018.  Increase PMTCT coverage from 39% to 90% of HIV positive pregnant women by 2018.  Maintain the prevalence of HIV positive pregnant women under 3% until 2018.  Reduce the rate of vertical transmission below 5% by 2018</narrative>
  </description>
